<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>How to Calculate Age from Date of Birth | SmartToolz</title><meta name="description" content="Learn how age is calculated from a date of birth, why calendar dates matter, and how to get a clear years, months and days result."><link rel="canonical" href="https://smarttoolz.in/blog/how-to-calculate-age-from-date-of-birth/"><?php require dirname(__DIR__) . '/head.php'; ?></head><body><?php require dirname(__DIR__) . '/header.php'; ?><main class="container py-5" style="max-width:900px"><article><span class="eyebrow">CALCULATOR GUIDE</span><h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mt-3">How to Calculate Age from Date of Birth</h1><p class="lead text-muted">Age looks simple, but calendar boundaries make an exact years-and-months calculation different from simply subtracting two years.</p><h2>How age is normally calculated</h2><p>Start with the date of birth and compare it with the target date. Completed years are counted first. If the birthday has not occurred yet in the target year, one year is subtracted from the simple year difference.</p><h2>Why months and days need calendar logic</h2><p>Months have different lengths, and February can contain 28 or 29 days. An exact age result therefore needs to work with the actual calendar dates rather than treating every month as the same number of days.</p><h2>Example</h2><p>Suppose someone was born on 15 May 2000 and the target date is 7 September 2026. Their completed years are determined from the May birthday, then the remaining period is counted in calendar months and days. This is more precise than dividing a total number of days by 365.</p><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Using only the difference between birth years.</li><li>Ignoring whether the birthday has happened this year.</li><li>Treating every year as exactly 365 days.</li><li>Mixing date formats such as day-month-year and month-day-year.</li></ul><h2>Calculate an age quickly</h2><p>Enter the birth date and the target date in the <a href="/tools/age-calculator/">SmartToolz Age Calculator</a> to get a clear calendar-based result without doing the date arithmetic manually.</p><h2>Practical tip</h2><p>For forms, records and reports, keep the original date in a consistent format and state the target date used for the calculation. That makes the result reproducible.</p></article></main><?php require dirname(__DIR__) . '/footer.php'; ?></body></html>
